GreenFlag Web Application (Phase 3 - Cloud Deployment)
This guide explains how to deploy the GreenFlag web application on the DLSU CCS Cloud Server. It covers connecting to the virtual machine, configuring SSH access, installing the required software, setting up the database, uploading the project files, and running the application.
__________________________________________________________________
Server Information
Access the DLSU CCS Cloud portal:
https://ccscloud.dlsu.edu.ph/
Login using the credentials given to you
Realm: Proxmox VE authentication server
After logging in:
Open Datacenter → tala.
Select your assigned LXC Machine.
Click Console.
Login as root using the password above.
Note: It is normal if the password does not appear while typing.
__________________________________________________________________
System Requirements
Install the following packages on the server:
Apache2
PHP
MariaDB
SQLite3
PHP MySQL Extension
PHP SQLite Extension
PHP GD Extension
PHP MBString Extension
PHP DOM Extension
__________________________________________________________________
Installation & Deployment Guide
Step 1: Update the Server
Run the following commands:
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade
sudo apt full-upgrade
__________________________________________________________________
Step 2: Create an SSH User
Create a new user by running:
sudo adduser user_name
Replace "user_name" with your preferred username.
Choose a password and press Enter to skip the remaining optional information.
__________________________________________________________________
Step 3: Enable SSH Access
Allow SSH and Apache through the firewall.
sudo ufw allow ssh
sudo ufw allow "Apache"
Enable the firewall.
sudo ufw enable
Verify that the firewall is active.
sudo ufw status
The status should display "active".
__________________________________________________________________
Step 4: Connect Using SSH
On your own computer, connect to the server using:
ssh user_name@ccscloud.dlsu.edu.ph -p 604##
Replace:
user_name with the account you created.
604## with your assigned SSH port.
To disconnect from the server, type:
logout
__________________________________________________________________
Step 5: Install Required Packages
Install Apache, PHP, MariaDB, SQLite, and the required PHP extensions.
sudo apt install apache2 php libapache2-mod-php php-mysql mariadb-server sqlite3 php-sqlite3 php-gd php-mbstring php-dom
If prompted, enter your password.
If you receive the message:
this user_name is not in the sudoers file. This incident will be reported.
continue to the troubleshooting section below.
__________________________________________________________________
Step 6: Verify Apache Installation
Open the following address in your browser:
http://ccscloud.dlsu.edu.ph:[HTTP_PORT]
Replace [HTTP_PORT] with your assigned HTTP port.
If Apache is installed successfully, the default Apache page should appear.
__________________________________________________________________
Step 7: Create the Project Directory
Navigate to the web directory.
cd /var/www/html
Create your project folder.
mkdir your_project_folder
Example:
sudo mkdir /var/www/html/T1-GreenFlag
__________________________________________________________________
Database Setup
Step 1: Secure MariaDB
Run:
sudo mysql_secure_installation
Use the following responses:
Switch to unix_socket authentication? n
Change the root password? n
Remove anonymous users? y
Disallow root login remotely? y
Remove test database and access to it? y
Reload privilege tables now? y
__________________________________________________________________
Step 2: Restart MariaDB
sudo service mysql restart
__________________________________________________________________
Step 3: Configure the Firewall
Allow the required ports.
sudo ufw allow 80
sudo ufw allow 3306
sudo ufw allow 80/tcp
sudo ufw allow 60135/tcp
sudo ufw allow "Apache"
sudo ufw reload
Restart the server.
sudo reboot
__________________________________________________________________
Step 4: Create the Database
Login to MariaDB.
mysql -u root -p
Display the available databases.
SHOW DATABASES;
Create your database.
CREATE DATABASE testDb;
Replace "testDb" with your preferred database name.
Verify the database.
SHOW DATABASES;

__________________________________________________________________
Uploading the Web Application
Step 1: Install FileZilla
Download and install FileZilla from:
https://filezilla-project.org/
__________________________________________________________________
Step 2: Configure FileZilla
Open FileZilla.
Go to File → Site Manager.
Create a new site using the following settings:
Protocol: SFTP - SSH File Transfer Protocol
Host: ccscloud.dlsu.edu.ph
Port: 604##
Username: Your created user account (not root)
Password: Your user account password
Click Connect.
__________________________________________________________________
Step 3: Upload the Project Files
After connecting:
The left panel shows your local computer.
The right panel shows the CCS Cloud server.
Navigate to:
/var/www/html/your_project_folder/
Replace "your_project_folder" with the folder you created earlier (for example, T1-GreenFlag).
Drag and drop all GreenFlag project files from your local computer into this folder.
__________________________________________________________________
Step 4: Access the Application
Open your browser and navigate to:
http://ccscloud.dlsu.edu.ph:[HTTP_PORT]/your_project_folder/
Replace:
[HTTP_PORT] with your assigned HTTP port.
your_project_folder with the folder you uploaded.
__________________________________________________________________
Troubleshooting
User Cannot Use sudo
If you receive:
this user_name is not in the sudoers file.
This incident will be reported.
Login to the VM using the browser console as root and run:
usermod -aG sudo user_name
Reconnect using SSH:
ssh user_name@ccscloud.dlsu.edu.ph -p 604##
Then update the package list:
sudo apt update
__________________________________________________________________
Cloud Page Times Out
If reopening the cloud page results in a timeout, temporarily disable the firewall.
sudo ufw disable
__________________________________________________________________
Notes
The SQL script provided by the professor contains several commands that are no longer supported by newer versions of MariaDB.
The following commands still work:
CREATE USER
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES
FLUSH PRIVILEGES
QUIT
The following commands produce ERROR 1064 because they are deprecated:
ALTER USER ... IDENTIFIED WITH auth_socket BY 'password';
SET PASSWORD FOR ... = PASSWORD("password");
This behavior is expected for:
root@localhost
root@192.168.%.%
root@10.%.%.%
No changes are required unless instructed otherwise.
__________________________________________________________________
Deployment Complete
After completing the steps above, you should have:
Access to the VM through SSH
Apache installed and running
PHP installed
MariaDB configured
Firewall configured
Project directory created
GreenFlag project uploaded
Database created
Application accessible through your assigned HTTP port


